  "title": "Breaking: Push Notifications API Removed",
  "summary": "The `channels.stop` method and the `Channel` schema have been removed from the Cloud Storage API. This is a breaking change that impacts any integrations relying on the push notification mechanism for resource change watches.",
  "details": "The `resources.channels.methods.stop` method, previously used to stop watching resources via push notifications, has been entirely removed. Correspondingly, the `Channel` schema, which defined the structure for these notification channels, including properties like `address`, `expiration`, `id`, `kind`, `params`, `payload`, `resourceId`, `resourceUri`, `token`, and `type`, has also been removed. Developers using Cloud Storage push notifications will need to update their applications as this functionality is no longer available through this API.",
